# Windsurf Rules — MetaBridge AI

The single source of truth for this repo is AGENTS.md. Follow it. This file mirrors the
non-negotiables so Windsurf/Cascade always enforces them.

WORKFLOW (every session, in order):
1. Read CHANGELOG.md first (Done / In Progress / Next).
2. Read + update the relevant spec in docs/specs/ BEFORE writing code (spec-first).
3. Create/append a task in docs/tasks/.
4. Implement to match the spec.
5. Update CHANGELOG.md last (move to Done, add Next).
6. Ensure lint + typecheck + tests pass.

Rule of thumb: No code without a spec. No work without a task. No session without reading the changelog.

ARCHITECTURE (loose coupling is law):
- Modules: auth, users, organizations, ecommerce, meta, ai, coupons, crm, conversations, analytics, reports, notifications.
- Never import another module's internals. Cross-module communication = public contract
  (application service / port) or DOMAIN EVENTS only. No circular dependencies.
- DDD layering per module: Presentation -> Application -> Domain <- Infrastructure.
  Dependencies point inward. Domain layer is PURE (no Prisma, fetch, env, framework).
- Repository pattern for all persistence. Event-driven across module boundaries.
- eCommerce/AI providers behind interfaces: adding a provider = implement the interface only.

CODING STANDARDS:
- TypeScript strict everywhere. No `any`, no `@ts-ignore`, no dynamic property access hacks.
- Naming: camelCase vars/functions, PascalCase types/components, SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE consts,
  kebab-case files (PascalCase.tsx for React components).
- Imports at top of file only. Access other modules via their public barrel, never deep imports.
- Validated config module for env; never scatter process.env. Never log/commit secrets or PII.
- Prisma migrations for all schema changes. Prefer deps published >=7 days ago; no floating ranges.
- Do not edit tests just to make them pass.

Full detail: AGENTS.md (§0–§7) and docs/architecture/.
